-- title:
--   Determinants on the twisted centralizer are scalar; unit-determinant part is compact open
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L$ a $K$-algebra of degree $\operatorname{finrank}_K L = 2$, and let $\sigma$ be a $K$-algebra automorphism of $L$ such that every $K$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $L$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma$ (its integer powers). Fix a height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_K$, write $K_v$ for the $v$-adic completion and $E = L \otimes_K K_v$, and let $c \in K_v^\times$ and $\delta \in \mathrm{GL}_2(E)$. Assume `IsNormOf` holds for the scalar matrix $c$ and $\delta$, i.e. there is $y \in \mathrm{GL}_2(E)$ with the image of the scalar matrix $c$ under $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v) \to \mathrm{GL}_2(E)$ equal to $y^{-1} \cdot (\mathrm{normString}\ \sigma\ \delta) \cdot y$, where `normString` is the twisted norm element attached to $\delta$ and $\sigma$; assume also that for no unit $z$ of $E$ is $\delta$ $\sigma$-conjugate to the scalar matrix $z$, i.e. there is no $x$ with $\mathrm{scalar}(z) = x^{-1}\,\delta\,\sigma_{\mathrm{GL}}(x)$, $\sigma_{\mathrm{GL}}$ being the automorphism of $\mathrm{GL}_2(E)$ induced by $\sigma \otimes \mathrm{id}$. Then three assertions hold for the twisted centralizer $T = \{t : t\,\delta\,\sigma_{\mathrm{GL}}(t)^{-1} = \delta\}$: first, every $t \in T$ has $\det t$ equal to the image of some $s \in K_v^\times$ under the unit map of $\mathrm{includeRight} : K_v \to E$; second, the subset of $T$ consisting of those $t$ whose determinant comes in this way from an $s$ with $\mathrm{Valued.v}(s) = 1$ is open in $T$; and third, that same subset is compact.
--
--   Under the stated hypotheses the twisted centralizer of $\delta$ is the unit group of a quaternion division algebra over $K_v$, with reduced norm given by the determinant; the statement records that this norm takes values in $K_v^\times$ and that the subgroup of elements of determinant of valuation $1$ is a compact open subgroup. It feeds the local computations of twisted orbital integrals, being used by the results on the maximal-order twisted commutant, on the integral over the determinant shells, and on positivity and finiteness of the relevant measures.
